__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
tests/
database/app.db
.git/
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# Same allowlist as .gitignore's models/* rule, mirrored here on purpose -
# .dockerignore governs the build context independently of what git tracks,
# so without this, every self-registered tenant's model dir that happens to
# exist on whoever's machine runs `docker build` (dev/test artifacts from
# local training runs, none of them meant to ship) gets baked into the
# image right alongside the real Telco/Banking ones. Caught by actually
# building the image and inspecting it, not assumed correct - see
# docker-compose.yml's comment on the models/ volume for why an EMPTY
# models/ build context here would be just as wrong (Telco/Banking need to
# still be present) as an unfiltered one.
models/*
!models/v1/
!models/v1_enriched/
!models/v2/
!models/banking_v1/

# Not read at build time or by the running app - frontend has its own,
# separate .dockerignore/Dockerfile; node_modules/dist would only bloat the
# backend image's build context for no reason.
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/

# Unrelated large datasets and runtime-generated tenant uploads - same
# reasoning as .gitignore's own exclusions for these.
data/raw/olist_orders_dataset.csv
data/raw/olist_order_payments_dataset.csv
data/tenant_uploads/
data/live_demo/
data/live_demo_v2/
data/test_onboarding_samples/
